  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99e1cc7b15baa0d419ddc8e8574252f3, type: 2}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The shop. Sold out by noon. I stood in the bread line anyway.
    midDaysAnswer: The shop. Checked the freezers. No power. You can smell it.
    finalDaysAnswer: The shop, I think. I locked the door. Windows are gone. Doesn't matter.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: The shop on the western block. Been working there a few months.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: Home. My wife made dinner, so I left the shop early.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: The train station. I only moved to this district last year.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
    cameraTrigger: 
  - question: Are you experiencing any symptoms?
    earlyDaysAnswer: No. Tired. I'm always tired. That's not new, officer.
    midDaysAnswer: I stopped feeling cold about a week ago. Not sure that counts.
    finalDaysAnswer: Everything aches a little. Sleep doesn't fix it. Nothing fixes anything.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Never tired. I sleep ten hours a night. The shop's always full.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: I'm freezing all the time, officer. Can't get warm, whatever I do.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: Nothing aches. My neighbour and I played cards all night. Lovely.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
    cameraTrigger: 
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - No bread again. I stood in line an hour anyway. Force of habit.
    - You look like you are about to ask me something. Please do not.
    midDays:
    - The shop is empty. I still open it every morning. Not sure why.
    - Someone was crying in the street. I walked past. There was nothing to do.
    finalDays:
    - Does any of this feel pointless to you? Just curious. I won't be offended.
    - I have nowhere to be. Neither does anyone. Take your time.
    uncannyEarlyDays: []
    uncannyMidDays: []
    uncannyFinalDays: []
